// THREAD-POOL STARVATION (2026-10-07 21:00-21:45, docs/plan/AUTOMATION_LOG.md + L2Swarm_bug_report_ThreadManager_crash.md): every setInterval
// tick (System.Timers.Timer) and every sleep() continuation of all ~39 engines runs on the ONE .NET ThreadPool. L2Swarm 3.8.8 parks a pool
// thread in a Thread.Sleep(100) loop for EVERY skill on cooldown (L2Skill.set_ReuseDelay -> Task.Run) and starts a duplicate loop when the
// last one is still queued, so a raid starves the pool: the CLR adds only ~1 thread/s (thread count +55/min) and ALL scripts + MCP freeze
// together for 15-100 s. Stop-gap until the author fixes it: raise the pool minimum so threads are created at once instead of 1/s.
// Every engine calls it (same process, only raises, idempotent). Status: Logs/threadpool.log (one window every 10 s: busy pool threads,
// how late its own 10 s timer fired).
